Dialogue: 0,0:00:00.32,0:00:03.15,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}First fix: draw a hill map, not arrows,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:03.23,0:00:06.80,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}and let the {\c&HE58739&}flow{\c&HF7F4F2&} run\Nalong its contour lines.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:06.88,0:00:09.64,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Where the lines crowd, it runs faster,
Dialogue: 0,0:00:09.72,0:00:13.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}so nothing piles up or leaks,\Nwhatever the landscape.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:13.98,0:00:16.79,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The box agrees: lines in, lines out.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:17.66,0:00:22.02,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}So the {\c&HF09CB4&}machine{\c&HF7F4F2&} draws two hill maps,\Nfor the flow and the field:
Dialogue: 0,0:00:22.10,0:00:26.73,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}zero divergence by construction,\Nhowever badly it is trained.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:27.60,0:00:33.60,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Second fix, for any field: split it into\Nswirl plus slope, and delete the slope.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:33.75,0:00:39.55,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Wave by wave, remove the part of each\Narrow along the wave's own direction.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:40.42,0:00:45.43,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}The gauges fall to rounding error,\Ndown to ten to the minus seventeen.
Dialogue: 0,0:00:45.51,0:00:49.90,Sub,,0,0,0,,{\fad(120,100)\move(960,1020,960,1016,0,120)}Measured, though, with the very\Noperator used to enforce it.
